# No test code in production source

Test-only helpers must not live in production `src/` packages.

## Where test helpers belong

| Repo | Test helper location |
|------|----------------------|
| NetworthSync, NetworthCSV, NetworthDB, NetworthDOM | `tests/` |
| NetworthJWT | `src/tests/` and `src/tests/support/` |

## Do not add to `src/`

- Functions or types named `*test*`, `*Test*`, `OpenForTest`, `reset_test_*`, `set_*_for_tests`
- Comments marking code as "for tests"
- Test auth bypasses, DB truncate helpers, JWKS injection hooks, or env-cache reset APIs

## Allowed in production `src/`

- Generic dependency injection (e.g. `assembleApp` with an auth hook parameter) when the API is not test-named and production uses it normally
- Framework-generated artifacts (e.g. Ent `enttest`)

## When adding test infrastructure

Put new helpers in the repo's `tests/` tree (or `src/tests/support/` for Go). Import production modules from tests; never the reverse for test-only behavior.
